# Trivy vulnerability ignore list.
#
# Entries are scoped to a specific advisory ID (never a blanket package or
# directory skip) so any *other* vulnerability in the same library still
# surfaces. Each entry records why it is not actionable for us.

# rustls 0.23.42 -> 0.23.45 (GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc, MEDIUM).
# rustls is a transitive Rust dependency compiled into the prebuilt `temporalio`
# Python wheel's native bridge (temporalio/bridge). The pinned rustls version is
# controlled by the Temporal SDK maintainers; as of temporalio 1.34.0 (the
# latest release) the bundled bridge still locks rustls 0.23.42, so there is no
# upstream wheel we can bump to in order to clear it. The bridge's rustls is
# used only for the appliance's outbound, authenticated TLS connection to its
# own Temporal server (not untrusted network input). Re-evaluate and remove this
# line when a temporalio release ships rustls >= 0.23.45.
GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc
